  "articleBody": "It's super frustrating when you're trying to install new molding in your bathroom, and it just won't stay put. Often, the culprit is inadequate surface preparation. You might think a quick wipe-down is enough, but for good adhesion, that surface needs to be absolutely clean and dry. Any old adhesive, soap scum, or even dust can prevent new molding from bonding properly. Also, consider the type of adhesive you're using. Not all glues are created equal, especially in a humid bathroom environment. You'll want something specifically designed for moisture resistance and strong bonding. Another common issue is not applying enough pressure during installation or not letting the adhesive cure for the recommended time. Many silicones and construction adhesives need a solid 24 to 72 hours to achieve full water resistance and strength. Trying to rush the process can lead to the molding detaching prematurely. Don't forget about sealing the edges with waterproof caulk; this isn't just for aesthetics, it's crucial for keeping moisture out and helping secure the molding. If you've tried all of these steps and your molding still isn't cooperating, it might be time to call in a professional like HH Remodeling LLC. We can assess the situation, fix any underlying issues, and ensure your bathroom molding is installed correctly and securely.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
